  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'handmade-indigenous-beaded-corn-earrings-green-cream-seed-beads-real-corn-husks-', '4614101332', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4614101332/handmade-indigenous-beaded-corn-earrings?click_key=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%3ALT15ad8c715d9fd8410f7a4bba460a830e8a50ef5a&click_sum=9aa24f63&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-729084-8-48&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&content_source=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%253ALT15ad8c715d9fd8410f7a4bba460a830e8a50ef5a',
   'Handmade Indigenous Beaded Corn Earrings | Green & Cream Seed Beads | Real Corn Husks | 1.5" Dangle Earrings', 'Handmade Indigenous Beaded Corn Earrings | Green & Cream Seed Beads | Real Corn Husks | 1.5" Dangle Earrings Celebrate the beauty of Indigenous agricultural traditions with these unique, handcrafted beaded corn earrings. Inspired by the sacred significance of maize in Native American cultures, each miniature ear of corn features delicate green and cream seed beads, carefully arranged to resemble kernels nestled beneath a natural corn husk. Made with real dried corn husks, these earrings beautifully combine traditional agricultural materials with intricate beadwork. Gold-tone fishhook ear wires and wire-wrapped accents complete their earthy, elegant appearance. Measuring approximately 1.5 inches long, these lightweight earrings are perfect for everyday wear, harvest celebrations, cultural gatherings, or as a meaningful gift for someone who appreciates Indigenous artistry and food sovereignty. Details: - Length: Approximately 1.5 inches - Bead Colors: Green and cream - Materials: Seed beads, genuine dried corn husks, gold-tone findings - Design: Miniature ears of corn with natural husk detailing - Style: Indigenous-inspired, botanical, agricultural, and nature-inspired - Handmade with attention to detail More Than Jewelry Corn is more than a crop. Across many Indigenous nations, maize represents nourishment, resilience, reciprocity, and the enduring relationship between people and the land. These miniature beaded ears of corn offer a beautiful tribute to the seeds that have sustained generations. A wearable celebration of ancestral agriculture, seed keeping, and the beauty of the harvest. 🌽', 'turquoise-jewelry',
