  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'vintage-navajo-sterling-silver-ring-mother-of-pearl-cabochon-size-11-25-signed-d', '4388370666', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4388370666/vintage-navajo-sterling-silver-ring?click_key=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%3ALTff5a131a34c527778766cd65ec2cf6f75924234a&click_sum=84c0d000&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-729084-8-39&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&frs=1&sts=1&content_source=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%253ALTff5a131a34c527778766cd65ec2cf6f75924234a',
   'Vintage Navajo Sterling Silver Ring Mother of Pearl Cabochon Size 11.25 Signed Dayea', 'This exquisite 1970s statement ring features a shining white 27 mm x 18 mm Mother of Pearl cabochon bezel set in a beautifully crafted Sterling Silver shadowbox. The contemporary styled Sterling Silver perfectly frames the Shell, making this ring a standout piece for any jewelry collection. Marked ''MD'' by Navajo Silversmith Mary Dayea, this size 11.25 ring weighs a hefty 19.34 grams and has been independently tested as Sterling Silver. The top of the ring is 34.7 mm at its longest, tapering to 5.7 mm at the bottom of the band. This vintage ring displays a slight patina and has been cleaned but not polished. Mother of Pearl, a fascinating organic gemstone, is not a traditional mineral but rather the iridescent inner layer of Mollusk shells. Composed primarily of Aragonite, a form of calcium carbonate, it is a testament to the marvels of nature''s design. This luminous material is characterized by its mesmerizing nacreous sheen, which exhibits a delicate play of colors ranging from creamy white and silver to soft pinks, blues, and greens. Its formation is a slow, meticulous process, as the Mollusk secretes layers of nacre to protect itself from irritants, resulting in the lustrous, shimmering surface we cherish. Revered for its ethereal beauty and symbolic connection to the ocean, Mother of Pearl is often associated with purity, femininity, and emotional healing. Its versatility and gentle elegance make it a popular choice for jewelry and decorative items, offering a unique and timeless alternative to more conventional gemstones. ----SHIPPING INFORMATION---- We ship Monday through Friday, usually within 1 business day of receiving payment. Everything is shipped well-protected, so you should always receive your item in the same condition it left us. Unless required by customs for international buyers, we ship with no jewelry-related terms on the packaging for your protection and ours. We sometimes use repurposed padding to protect items during shipping and minimize our ', 'turquoise-jewelry',
