  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'vintage-1973-southwestern-indian-tribes-book-native-american-history-turquoise-j', '4613677374', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4613677374/vintage-1973-southwestern-indian-tribes?click_key=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%3ALT50c1a6654f496ca82b5d83f6b8ea9221e269158a&click_sum=47cc2418&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-729084-8-33&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&frs=1&sts=1&content_source=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%253ALT50c1a6654f496ca82b5d83f6b8ea9221e269158a',
   'Vintage 1973 Southwestern Indian Tribes Book | Native American History, Turquoise Jewelry, Pueblo Art & Photography', 'Handpicked by FloweringSageVintage Discover the rich artistic traditions and cultural history of the American Southwest in this beautifully illustrated book by Tom Bahti. Published by KC Publications, this 1973 fourth printing of Southwestern Indian Tribes features period photography, colorful examples of traditional jewelry, historic architecture, pottery, ceremonial objects, and Native American artwork. With its distinctive Southwestern-inspired cover design and richly illustrated pages, this paperback is a nice addition to a Southwestern book collection, home library, or collection of Native American art and history. Inside You''ll Find: • Beautiful photographs of turquoise and silver jewelry • Traditional Navajo, Hopi, Zuni, and Pueblo arts • Kachina dolls, pottery, beadwork, and ceremonial objects • Historic photographs of Southwestern landscapes and architecture • Cultural and historical information about numerous Southwestern tribes • Color and black-and-white illustrations throughout Details: • Author: Tom Bahti • Title: Southwestern Indian Tribes • Year: 1973 (Fourth Printing) • Original Copyright: 1968 • Publisher: KC Publications, Las Vegas, Nevada • Format: Staple binding, 12 x 9”, 72 pages • Language: English Condition: Good preowned condition with signs of age and handling, including some cover wear and light page aging. Owner’s label on front cover. The illustrated interior pages are still clean and bright. Binding is solid. Please review all listing photographs for condition details. Perfect for: Collectors of Southwestern Americana, Native American art enthusiasts, vintage book lovers, and anyone interested in the history and artistic heritage of the American Southwest. A charming piece of 1970s Southwestern publishing history! This is an authentic 1973 printing, not a reproduction. Historical terminology and perspectives reflect the period in which the book was written.', 'turquoise-jewelry',
