  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'vintage-red-coral-girls-ring-size-3-5-southwest-coin-silver-old-pawn-jewelry', '4614079548', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4614079548/vintage-red-coral-girls-ring-size-35?click_key=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%3ALT72968aef773a842ce93a45c0a61b58bd4ce2f49b&click_sum=bdaa5de4&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-729084-8-32&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&sts=1&content_source=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%253ALT72968aef773a842ce93a45c0a61b58bd4ce2f49b',
   'Vintage Red Coral Girls Ring Size 3.5 Southwest Coin Silver Old Pawn Jewelry', 'Red Coral Flower Ring Size 3.5 Vintage Southwest Trading Post Jewelry A perfect piece of southwestern cheer, this vintage ring is a lovely way to carry a desert bloom. Made from coin silver and a vibrant red coral cabochon, this ring band is a US size 3.25, which is well suited to a child''s hand or as a midi ring. The ring face measures 5/16" (15 mm) in diameter. It is unmarked but appears to be coin silver. Based on the style, I would say this was likely made for the tourist trade in the 1970s. The ring weighs 2 grams. It is in excellent vintage condition with minimals signs of age and previous wear. It still bears a sharpie mark on the back indicating the size of the band (though it fits more like a 3.25 because of the shape of the flower). I believe this ring has never been worn and is likely old stock from a trading post. Is it a gift? Need to buy a card? All cards ship free with purchase. http://www.etsy.com/shop/AdobeHouseVintage?section_id=13802190 Thanks so much for looking!', 'turquoise-jewelry',
