  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'handmade-navajo-pink-conch-pendant-in-sterling-silver-native-american-jewelry', '4376201960', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/4376201960/handmade-navajo-pink-conch-pendant-in?click_key=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%3ALT8e77f64e5ea9625231acc19f2e9b27cce4bc8585&click_sum=9d703fd6&ls=s&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-729084-8-31&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&frs=1&cns=1&sts=1&content_source=88861da3-e3d9-479a-bf79-3455fad45126%253ALT8e77f64e5ea9625231acc19f2e9b27cce4bc8585',
   'Handmade Navajo PINK CONCH Pendant in Sterling Silver - Native American Jewelry', 'Give a gift as special as she is with beautiful, one-of-a-kind handmade jewelry! PENDANT ONLY! NAVAJO Native American PINK CONCH Teardrop Pendant in Sterling Silver! One of a Kind Genuine Pink Conch Shell Navajo Handmade Pendant This one of a kind pendant looks great on Navajo Pearls. The bail would accommodate 6mm Navajo Pearls or smaller. Pair with Navajo Pearls and other Native American jewelry. Choose your desired pendant at checkout. NOTE: The Navajo Pearls pictured are for DISPLAY only and are not included. See all pics and video for measurements and additional details. About Pink Conch…Pink Conch Shell is a natural shell with swirls of pinks and creams. Colors and intensity will vary. Small pitting and indented striations can sometimes be seen in the shell. This is just part of the natural shell and is a matter of personal preference when choosing a piece of pink conch jewelry. Artist: Handmade by Navajo artist Jimson Berlin Retail Price: $300.00 Our Price: $175.00 Gram Weight: 10 Grams Shipping: FREE IMPORTANT NOTE: See the photos to verify the specifics of this beautiful jewelry. Keep in mind that all items are handmade and cannot be compared to traditional machine-made jewelry regarding uniformity. We believe this uniqueness is what makes each piece particularly beautiful and valuable. FOLLOW ME at https://www.facebook.com/BlueRockTurquoise to stay updated on new additions to our shop AND fun pics of our crazy lives... Our mission is to inspire a revolution of LOVE for handmade Native American Turquoise (and other stones) Jewelry! Join us in our OBSESSION for this beautiful and well-made jewelry. My sister and I (Kim and Phyllis) lived in Cloudcroft, NM as children. Phyllis and her husband Craig own Burro Street Trading Post in Cloudcroft and have a LIVE Facebook Jewelry show most Tuesdays at 6:00 p.m. Mountain Time. I manage the ETSY site for shoppers who prefer to shop online. Phyllis and Craig host the LIVE Facebook shows...and I make guest appearances!', 'turquoise-jewelry',
