  (uuid_generate_v4(), 'iris-arch-triangle-indian-navajo-inspired-steel-punches-jewelry-metal-leather-st', '1893280225', 'https://www.etsy.com/listing/1893280225/irisarchtriangle-indian-navajo-inspired?click_key=EuAGqaHVhY1NZyPS66SQ7bHMrZc5%3ALT0bbc77e5e05161a55af00400d4d246f1c448a15e&click_sum=77befcc2&ls=a&ga_order=most_relevant&ga_search_type=all&ga_view_type=gallery&ga_search_query=Navajo+jewelry&ref=search_grid-729083-8-12&sr_prefetch=1&pf_from=search&pro=1&sts=1',
   'Iris/Arch/Triangle Indian Navajo Inspired Steel Punches Jewelry Metal, Leather Stamping Tools Bracelet DIY Craft Tool, Jewelry Making Gift', 'Materials: Carbon Steel The stamp is made of high quality High-speed steel . Its made for strength and hardiness to insure the stamp is ready when you need it. The head of the stamp is made of the same quality steel and should give you the stamp every time. Size: 5mm; 7mm; 9mm We can customize stamps as your requests. If You need custom made punch stamp, please visit this listing: https://www.etsy.com/listing/4317051121/custom-metal-stamp-punch-tool-hand?ref=shop_home_active_1&pro=1&frs=1&sts=1&logging_key=813943293f2f87efd126b288927ad9f05554763f%3A4317051121 Suitable for stamping on Aluminum, Pewter, Alkeme, Copper, Nickel, Silver, Leather. Great stamping set for festival, birthday, anniversary handmade gift. FEATURES: *Stamp size in the listing depends on a widest side *High-carbon tool steel construction *Length of stamps steel rod: about 7-10cm for comfortable handling. *Stamps are made by deep laser engraving 0.8mm-1.5mm for crisp, clear impressions. *At least 60 HRC hardness after heat treatment. *Good for stamping softer metals like aluminum, silver, gold, etc., but alloy metal is not recommended. *Ideal for use with a hammer or hydraulic press for larger designs or complicated ones. *The stamp "can" be used on stainless steel, but it will not be easy, because stainless steel is a very hard metal, it is rather difficult to press. So, we do not recommend this metal for beginners. The larger or more complex the pattern is, the more difficult it is to print it in stainless steel. So, we highly recommend buying some aluminum blanks for practice. USAGE & MAINTENANCE of the stamps: *For punching use hammer and place the blank on a hard, smooth surface (the best metal, steel plate or anvil), don''t be afraid to hit hard to ensure a clean impression! (NOTE: Brass hammers do not fit for these stamps) *If the stamp gets rusty, brush it with simple hard sponge and boil it for 10 minutes in water with soda. *For bigger stamps or complicated ones, it can be hard to get the', 'turquoise-jewelry',
